WEBVTT

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:07.480
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:07.480
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.780
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.780
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:18.160
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:18.160
the only thing I truly have

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.450
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.450
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:28.790
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:28.790
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:34.050
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:34.050
the season of the coming summer began.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:39.430
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:39.430
I had begun to understand many things

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:45.520
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:45.520
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:51.070
garakuta no yama kara

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:51.070
In the junk I've piled up,

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:55.150
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:55.150
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:01:00.450
hibike kono koe yo

00:00:55.150 --> 00:01:00.450
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:06.710
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:06.710
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:12.380
namida kareru made

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:12.380
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:17.430
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:17.430
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:22.760
namida hareru made

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:22.760
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.770
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.770
though I may lose my way,

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:31.610
egakikake no ima

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:31.610
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:33.110
kizamu

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:38.860
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.400
akashi

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.860
kono te de

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.250
That was our third consecutive win against the Jets!

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.530
We're back to full strength.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.110
Yeah.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:49.240
Not to mention the crowds are getting bigger every day.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.930
However, we can't celebrate just yet.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.840
We must turn this momentum into profit.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.880
Call Shigeno up here.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.230
Shigeno?

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.640
An Uninvited Guest

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.640
An Uninvited Guest

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:10.060
Shigeno!

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.360
The savior of the Hornets!

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.410
Your performance hasn't just attracted attention from Japan,

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:18.030
you're a hero in both Japan and America!

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.990
Yeah, thanks...

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.700
So, what did you need me for?

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.120
Nice to meet you, Mr. Shigeno.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.290
I've always wanted to meet you.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.460
Is he Japanese?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.300
An advertising agency?

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.920
My name is Furuichi.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.970
He said he'd like to feature you in a Japanese commercial.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:46.560
Yes, your amazing pitching is all over the news in Japan.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.140
A company I work with said they'd love to have you do a commercial—

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:50.980
Get real!

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.790
This is a chance!

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.050
If more people hear about you through your commercials,

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.900
we'll get a much bigger Japanese audience.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.580
And of course, we'll pay you as much as we can for going on—

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.950
There's no way I could do that when we're just about to win in our division!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.160
Shigeno, you're talking to the owner.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.960
I don't work in the entertainment industry!

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.070
I'll do whatever you say regarding baseball,

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:14.210
but I don't have time for anything else!

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:15.920
Wait, Shigeno!

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.840
He's unbelievable...

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.550
My apologies, Mr. Furuichi.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.530
O-Oh, no.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:28.650
But... if he's so reluctant, we'll have to simply call this deal—

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.020
Please, hold on!

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.450
I'm sure he's simply overwhelmed by all this.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.890
We can definitely convince him!

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.690
I'll give you one week.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.680
My clients in Japan have their own schedule,

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.580
so I can't wait any longer than that.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:41.700
Very well.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.330
That's how it is.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.120
Understand?

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.780
This is going to be a pain...

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.170
Is something wrong?

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.600
Hi.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.050
Who put this training menu together?

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.090
Who?

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.780
I did.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.890
Are you trying to be a professional wrestler?

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:24.960
Huh?

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.420
I saw you working out,

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.770
and this is just too much weight for bench pressing.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:32.560
You're a pitcher, so you shouldn't build too much muscle.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.290
Wh-What did you say?

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.810
Who are you anyway?

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:38.210
Oh, I'm sorry about that.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.540
My name's Sophia Reed.{check last name}

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:42.090
I have something to talk to you about.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.260
Talk?

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:46.510
Yes, it's about the Japanese television commercial.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.600
I already declined that offer!

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.320
I'm asking you to reconsider it.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.900
There's nothing to reconsider!

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.080
Aren't you also part of the ball team?

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.600
Aren't you obligated to improve the image of—

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:00.440
Shut up!

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:03.970
No matter what you tell me, I have absolutely zero interest in commercials!

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.570
Don't ever talk to me again!

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.240
What in the world is his problem?!

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:20.590
Immediately after being promoted to the majors, he withdrew from the frontline.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:27.750
After being reinstated, he has gone against orders to continue pitching and has refused several interviews.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:32.280
I can already tell from reading this that he's quite self-centered.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.260
It's hard to believe he's a rookie.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:38.230
Featuring Shigeno in a commercial?

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.430
The owner is set on doing it.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.480
Are you sure?

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:42.980
The season isn't over yet.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.990
It should be fine as long as we only shoot on his days off.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:48.450
But how am I supposed to convince him when he's against it?

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.380
Don't worry, I believe in you, Sophia.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:52.730
O-Okay...

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:53.550
Thanks!

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.000
Oh, w-wait!

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.400
Basically, he forced his orders from the owner onto me!

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.160
Can I sit next to you?

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.160
Watts.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.120
It's rare to see you drinking alone.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.850
It happens.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:14.600
The usual.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.110
Talk about timing.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:21.080
I wanted to talk with someone from the team.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.130
Talk?

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:26.400
I want to know about Goro Shigeno.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.450
Shigeno?

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.240
A commercial for Shigeno?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.040
He's become quite popular.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.860
I know your job is to manage the players,

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:41.910
but negotiating to feature them in commercials...

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:43.580
That's tough.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:44.970
Negotiate?

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.610
I don't even want to talk to him face to face!

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.680
Wow, you really don't like him.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.890
I read his profile, and I can clearly say,

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.260
Goro Shigeno only thinks about himself.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.550
If you ask me, he's the worst player out there.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:04.860
Well, I guess that's understandable if you've only read about him.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.680
Have you ever seen his games live?

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:08.580
No.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:11.910
I've been traveling the world for other jobs this season.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:15.550
You've read a bunch of facts, but they're not the truth.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:16.790
What do you mean?

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.020
He isn't exactly smart.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:23.750
Quite frankly, he can only express himself through baseball.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.290
So he's easily misunderstood.

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.610
Are you implying I'm misunderstanding him?

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:30.630
If you want to know about Shigeno,

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:31.930
I suggest you stop reading about him...

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:35.760
and watch him play with your own eyes.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.790
He's starting in the next game, right?

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:42.760
Yeah.

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:45.690
Thanks.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:50.630
I'll see for myself if the Guardian of the Hornets speaks the truth.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.620
The Guardian, huh?

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:05.810
Your hip is looking a lot worse than I anticipated.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:09.650
I'm not absolutely sure without further inspection,

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:15.090
but at this rate, you may not be able to pitch to the end of the season.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.310
Pitcher, number 56:

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.330
Goro Shigeno!

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:35.200
...and watch him play with your own eyes.

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:39.540
If Shigeno's starting today, this game's ours.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.410
Yeah, once we get three runs, it's over.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:50.350
Strike out!

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:53.360
Strike out!

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.050
Strike out!

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:26.750
Strike out!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:28.170
Game over!

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:34.810
Indeed.

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:37.010
He's not at all like his profile says.

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:46.610
Morning!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.280
Wh-What are you doing here?

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:50.560
Hey, stop getting distracted!

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.190
You'll mess up your rhythm.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:56.750
E-Even if you follow me here, I still won't do the—

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.980
I'm not giving up until you say you will.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.280
Look...

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.700
And did you know? I'm also qualified as a conditioning coach.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:06.530
Conditioning?

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:07.620
What is that?

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:13.460
A job that helps players maintain or improve their health and keeps them free of injuries and illness.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.550
Basically, it's a job that manages the lives of the players.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:17.570
Wait a minute!

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:18.880
I don't need something like—

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.100
Don't worry.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:23.000
I received permission to be your coach for a while.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.930
Wh-What are you blabbering on about?

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:25.920
Come on!

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.100
Who said you could stop?

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.270
Who does she think she is?

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:40.390
Okay, let's move on to stretching!

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:41.280
You're here again!

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:44.200
Relax your body...

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.390
Breathe slowly...

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.620
Slowly...

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:56.510
My shoulder feels really light.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:57.380
Doesn't it?

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.860
You're quite impressive, condensing coach!

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:01.980
<i>Conditioning </i>coach!

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:04.020
Do you feel like doing the commercial now?

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:05.680
Not one bit.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:11.350
The Coyotes have tied the game, and they've still got men on second and third with just one out!

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.510
The Coyotes may turn this game around!

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.650
It's a hit!

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:25.260
Silva hits a magnificent RBI double!

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:28.820
Silva's doing really good!

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:31.820
It's going to be a tough competition with him on the Coyotes.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.170
Hi!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.720
Y-You're—

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:37.660
Have you had dinner?

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:39.090
No, not yet.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.710
Great!

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:42.070
I brought some ingredients.

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:42.760
Wai—

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.720
What do you think you're doing here?

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:48.890
You need to change your diet.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:51.580
You're always going out or getting something delivered, right?

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:53.740
That doesn't mean you can come barging into my home!

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:55.060
Don't worry.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:57.190
I'm also a nutritionist.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.510
That's not what I meant.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.640
It's good!

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:07.440
Right?

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:09.350
It's super well-balanced too.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:10.790
That's impressive.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.280
They're all easy to make, so I'll write out the recipes for you.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.470
Thanks, that'll come in handy.

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:17.540
And...

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.380
about the commercial...

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.290
H-Hey, what are you doing?

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.870
Thanks for cooking me dinner.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:25.700
See ya!

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:26.470
Wai—

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:31.180
That's not going to be enough to drive me away!

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:42.860
Your pitches are looking really good today.

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:45.530
Yeah, well...

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.720
Okay, last one.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.810
I can't possibly say it's thanks to her.

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:59.040
She'll start barking at me about the commercial.

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:04.120
One more set.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:05.820
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:18.570
Here.

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:19.560
Oh, thanks.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.210
So what's next?

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:25.430
I was wondering when you'd storm out on me like the first time I met you,

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:26.870
but you're actually doing as I say.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:30.780
I can't just shove a great coach away.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:35.500
To be frank, I've been feeling really good since you started coaching me.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.230
Right?

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:37.310
So can you do the commer—

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:39.650
No, that has nothing to do with training.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:41.620
Why are you so stubborn?

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:46.890
Even if you coach me to make me feel like I owe you, I still won't do the commercial.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:48.230
That's not the only reason I'm coaching you.

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:48.720
Huh?

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:53.500
I hate to admit it, but you have amazing talent as a baseball player.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:57.030
If you train well, you still have a lot of room for growth.

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:59.320
You've made me want to help you as a coach.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.570
Well, what an honor.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.890
Isn't that Sophia, who keeps all the players in check?

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:12.670
Why's she giving private coaching to Shigeno?

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:13.410
I don't know.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:14.290
Damn it!

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.360
I was going after Sophia.

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:18.240
I don't think that's the problem here.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:26.000
Is Shigeno still saying no?

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.140
Y-Yes...

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:29.170
I have someone talking him into it, but...

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:30.180
Are you an idiot?!

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:34.070
I have to give the agent a reply within two days!

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:37.390
If this doesn't turn out well, you're shouldering all the blame!

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.060
O-Okay...

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.440
You sneaky little you!

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:44.650
What are you talking about?

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:45.940
Hey, Shigeno.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.860
When did you get so close to Sophia?

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:50.820
Th-That's not how it is!

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.450
She's talking you into doing a commercial?

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.100
Companies in Japan sure have weird taste.

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:01.630
Yeah, no doubt about that.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.550
Yeah...

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:04.170
Wait, what?

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:08.080
And when I declined the offer, it somehow turned out like this.

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:09.070
I'm completely lost!

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:12.390
You say that now, but you actually enjoy her company, don't you?

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:14.220
She's pretty cute, too.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:15.560
Are you kidding me?

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.340
She's just a nuisance!

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.140
I'm gonna shoo her away next time she comes near me!

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:27.610
What are you taking your time for?

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:30.780
Flatter him or even threaten him if you need to!

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.190
I really need you to get Shigeno to do the commercial!

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:36.700
But I would need his full consent.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:40.860
I can't have him lose his loyalty to the team over something this trivial.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:43.960
You have to understand that he's, above all, a baseball player!

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.930
I know that!

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:46.950
Please!

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:50.600
If the commercial gets called off, both you and I may be in danger of being fired.

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.200
Yes, I...

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:55.040
Make sure you convince him by tomorrow.

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:57.760
I'm really counting on you, Sophia.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:05.270
You're late.

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.440
I thought you weren't gonna be here today.

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:13.700
I had some work I needed to finish.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.010
You don't need to push yourself so hard.

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:17.550
Oh, I don't think so.

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:20.120
I plan to train you really hard for the entire day.

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:22.790
The entire day, huh?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.250
Wh-What about it?

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:25.310
Nothing.

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:26.450
So...

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:28.900
What should I start with, Coach?

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:31.550
O-Oh, continue stretching.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.560
One more set.

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:43.600
Why are you taking a break?

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:48.920
Say, why do I have to feature in a commercial?

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:51.280
What are you asking out of the blue?

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:57.360
My job is to show my best pitching possible in front of all the fans at the stadium,

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:58.250
so...

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.810
why would I need to do some stupid commercial?

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:02.860
The answer's quite simple.

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:04.720
It's because you're a major leaguer.

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:05.410
What?

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:06.640
Were you listening?

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:10.710
Isn't that precisely why the most important thing is to show the fans a good game?

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:12.610
It isn't just about the games.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:18.240
Players who make magnificent plays are the dreams and the heroes of all the fans.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.310
No matter how you see yourself.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:25.210
There are fans who can't come to the stadium,

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:28.040
even though they want to feel close to the Hornets all the time.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:33.580
I think returning those fans' feelings is also part of a major leaguer's job.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.950
I see.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.300
Okay, no more chitchat.

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:40.390
Let's get back to training.

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:50.710
I'm surprised you changed your mind.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.900
After what you said, I didn't have a choice.

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:57.010
After all, I'm a major leaguer.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.800
Thank you for waiting.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.810
Let's get him ready for the shooting.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.830
Okay.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:13.440
The plan is for you to drink this soda and then power up.

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:15.490
Power up, huh?

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.720
If only it were that easy.

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:18.800
Shigeno!

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:20.910
I know! Keep it down.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:24.010
Then I'd like you to knock the batter down.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.050
Where's the catcher?

00:18:26.050 --> 00:18:28.080
Do I just throw into the net?

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:31.080
No, just hit the mannequin's head.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:32.320
Head?

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:35.420
Yes, we'll replace it with someone else on the computer.

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.390
Is something wrong?

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:41.960
I quit!

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:43.430
Wh-What do you mean?

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:45.350
I'm saying I'm not doing this!

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:46.390
Say that again?

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.560
What exactly is going on?

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.720
What's gotten into you?

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:55.610
We were all ready to start the shooting.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:58.730
I already said I'd do it, so I was prepared to do anything.

00:18:58.730 --> 00:18:59.570
But...

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:05.410
Even if it's just a mannequin, I don't want to aim at the batter!

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:12.250
Right, your dad died from...

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:15.100
Sorry, Sophia.

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:17.800
I'm going to have to call this off.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:20.220
Mr. Shigeno!

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.350
Are you going to blow off the shooting?

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:24.100
Mr. Furuichi, please let me explain.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:24.880
There's a good reason he's not—

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:27.420
He's already signed the contract!

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:29.560
How are you going to explain yourself to Mr. Lance?

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:30.980
W-Well...

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.690
All right, I'll do it.

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.240
But, Shigeno...

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:44.160
Now that I think about it, I was wrong to get so worked up about a mannequin.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.450
Th-Then shall we get back to the shooting?

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.040
Ready, and action!

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:14.770
You of all people can't do that!

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.150
Sophia?

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.170
Miss Reed!

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:19.360
What do you think you're doing?

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:22.280
I'm putting an end to this shooting.

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:24.320
C-Cut the joke!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.700
You have no right to call this off!

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:30.110
I can't let a player forcibly go through with what he doesn't want to do!

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:34.640
Look, we went through with this plan with Mr. Lance's strong support!

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:35.610
Do you think you'll get away with—

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:36.710
Sure!

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.520
Tell the owner whatever you want!

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:39.050
What?

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:44.060
I cannot approve of something that will leave the impression of a pitch being dangerous to the viewers!

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:49.670
As one in charge of the Hornets... No, as a person related to baseball itself!

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:56.900
Sophia?

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:01.770
You really let them have it.

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:03.150
I think better of you now.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.820
Yeah, and same goes for you.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:09.120
You decided to do the commercial for my sake.

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:11.370
It looks like I misunderstood you.

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.190
Th-That's not why I...

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:14.350
Oh, darn.

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:16.990
It's unfortunate that I can't coach you anymore.

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:17.670
You can't?

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:23.180
I only received permission to be your private coach to talk you into the commercial.

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:25.650
So what about the next shooting?

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:31.630
I won't be there, but I'm sure you'll do fine since they said it won't be about baseball.

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:33.340
I'm looking forward to it, Shigeno.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.270
Which one? The commercial or baseball?

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:39.200
Isn't that obvious?

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:42.730
Yeah.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:49.390
Goodness...

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:51.790
He doesn't contact me at all.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:54.990
No news is good news, don't you know?

00:21:54.990 --> 00:21:56.460
I do know that!

00:21:56.840 --> 00:22:01.040
But I wish he'd at least let me hear his voice from time to time...

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.300
Let's do this with a bang!

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:03.990
Sis, look at this...

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:24.390
Quench your thirst with this fastball down your throat!

00:22:24.390 --> 00:22:26.840
Super Cider works, no doubt!

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:34.560
Wh-What is he doing...?

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:37.550
A-At least you got to hear his voice.

00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:51.170
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:51.170
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:57.890
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:57.890
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:58.100 --> 00:22:59.560
yume wo

00:22:58.100 --> 00:23:02.730
You were chasing your dream.

